      "title": "Content",
      "content": [
        "# Terminal Troubleshooting Guide for Cursor\r",
        "\r",
        "## Current Issues\r",
        "- Terminal in Cursor gets stuck or shows buffer errors\r",
        "- PowerShell commands with operators like `&&` fail\r",
        "- Console output formatting issues\r",
        "\r",
        "## Potential Solutions\r",
        "\r",
        "### 1. Switch from PowerShell to CMD\r",
        "We've already created a `.cursorrules` file that configures Cursor to use cmd.exe instead of PowerShell. This should help with compatibility issues, especially with commands that use operators like `&&`.\r",
        "\r",
        "```json\r",
        "{\r",
        "  \"terminal\": {\r",
        "    \"shell\": \"cmd.exe\",\r",
        "    \"args\": []\r",
        "  }\r",
        "}\r",
        "```\r",
        "\r",
        "### 2. Avoid Complex Terminal Commands in Cursor\r",
        "- Use batch files for complex operations instead of typing them directly in Cursor's terminal\r",
        "- Create and run scripts outside of Cursor for terminal-intensive tasks\r",
        "- Use the sync batch files we've created for WordPress file synchronization\r",
        "\r",
        "### 3. Use External Terminal for Complex Commands\r",
        "- Open an external Command Prompt or PowerShell window for complex operations\r",
        "- Run commands there instead of in Cursor's integrated terminal\r",
        "\r",
        "### 4. Update Cursor\r",
        "- Check for Cursor updates as newer versions might fix terminal integration issues\r",
        "- Visit [Cursor's website](https://cursor.sh/) for the latest version\r",
        "\r",
        "### 5. Alternative Approaches\r",
        "- Use Git Bash if available, which often has better compatibility\r",
        "- Configure VSCode as an alternative editor when terminal operations are needed\r",
        "\r",
        "## Testing Terminal Fix\r",
        "After applying the `.cursorrules` file, restart Cursor and try these test commands:\r",
        "\r",
        "```\r",
        "echo Hello World\r",
        "cd C:\\Users\\Chris\\cFish.io && dir\r",
        "```\r",
        "\r",
        "If successful, the terminal should execute both commands without errors.\r",
        "\r",
        "## For Future Development\r",
        "Consider implementing the WordPress file synchronization as part of your Git workflow:\r",
        "- Create a Git hook that automatically syncs files to WordPress Studio after commits\r",
        "- Create a GitHub Action to deploy changes to WordPress Studio on push to specific branches"
      ]
    }
  ],
